  FAIL: the STAKED two-resource form (max under --overlap, sum without) does NOT clear its kill rule.
  KILL RULE FIRED.  M2 does NOT get wired into quantprobe.  Per prereg section 5, the pre-declared fallback is evaluated next and published either way:
    two-resource ACCOUNTING survives: YES (N3 = C+I always, LOMO median 4.04% against 31.92% for the best one-resource null)
    the part that dies is the COMBINE RULE: --overlap does not turn sum into max.  Fitting a partial-overlap credit gives phi=0.180 and still does not beat phi=0 held-out (8.61% vs 4.04%).
    WHAT THAT FALLBACK PASS IS AND IS NOT (adversarial review 2026-07-30):
      - N3 was named as the fallback AFTER the arithmetic had been run (prereg section 0), so its pass is a SELECTION, not a prediction.  Two of its four gates cannot fail for it: K-3 asks whether it is the best same-cost form, which is why it was chosen, and K-4's bracketing conjunct is the mediant identity for an additive form.
      - What survives that is real: K-1 (LOMO max 28.66% < 35%), K-2 (8.07% < 31.92%), and K-4's tolerance half, which N3 clears on 4/5 pairs - pass_count stays 4 for any tolerance in (6.67%, 18.31%].
      - Wiring N3 in therefore still requires the separate commit prereg section 5 demands, and inherits every caveat in sections 7 and 8.
